---
import { orgPaths } from '../../../lib/tenant-paths';
export const getStaticPaths = orgPaths;

import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../../../components/PageHead.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Accessibility"
  description="What this site commits to, where it is verified, and how to report a barrier."
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="Policies"
    title="Accessibility"
    lede="A site that publishes student science is no use to a student who cannot read it. These are commitments, not aspirations, and several are checked automatically on every build."
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What we commit to</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Every text and background pair meets WCAG AA contrast at minimum, in every theme. This is asserted in the build and a failure stops the deploy.</li>
        <li>Body text is set at 18 pixels, and nothing anywhere is smaller than the floor recorded in the design system.</li>
        <li>Every interactive element has a visible keyboard focus ring, and nothing on the site requires a mouse or depends on hover.</li>
        <li>Headings follow a real hierarchy, so a screen reader can navigate by structure.</li>
        <li>Every figure carries alt text, and that is one of the checks that blocks a submission.</li>
        <li>Motion is close to absent, and what exists respects a reduced motion preference.</li>
        <li>The layout works down to a 360 pixel screen and reflows rather than scrolling sideways.</li>
        <li>Search is an accelerator, never the only route: every record is reachable from a static list that works with scripts turned off.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where it is weaker</h2>
      <p>
        Records that exist only as a scanned or image based PDF are not readable by a screen
        reader. Where we hold the text, we publish a full HTML version alongside the PDF, and
        that is the version this site is built around. Older material that arrived as a PDF
        only is the gap, and converting it is ordinary manual work rather than a technical
        problem.
      </p>
      <p>
        Equations are rendered as text rather than pictures wherever the source allows it.
        Where an author supplied an equation as an image, it carries a description.
      </p>

      <h2>Reporting a barrier</h2>
      <p>
        If any part of this site is unusable with a screen reader, a keyboard, at a text size
        you need, or in any other way, that is a defect. Write to
        <a href="/contact/">the contact address</a> and describe what you were trying to do.
        We will tell you what we are doing about it and roughly when.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
